  "id": "definitely-not-floating-grease-chronicles",
  "name": "Definitely Not Floating Grease Chronicles",
  "sortId": 166910,
  "sourceUrl": "https://honkai-star-rail.fandom.com/wiki/Definitely_Not_Floating_Grease_Chronicles",
  "scrapedAt": "2026-08-30T12:21:08.250Z",
  "volumes": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "volumeKey": "text",
      "label": "Text",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "If you are the greatest treasure hunter in the world,\nthen congratulations,\nyou have obtained the most precious fortune in this universe:\nan alchemy recipe.\nCommit it to your memory, and never let it go."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-9c5ef71bbc66f182"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Ingredients:"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Two ripe red tomatoes,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "three fresh eggs,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "15ml of refined vegetable oil,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "3g of salt,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "2g of white sugar,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "and one green onion."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-92fce29c1b209ed7"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Synthesis Process:"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Core the tomatoes and cut lengthwise,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "slice into crescent-shapred wedges,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "crack the eggs into a bowl,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "beat the eggs until smooth,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "finely chop the green onions and set aside,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "place pan over high heat,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "coat the pan evenly with oil;"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Once the oil is hot, pour in the egg mixture, gently swirl and spread flat;"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Transfer the naturally solidified egg pieces to a plate and set aside;"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Return the pan to high heat, add tomato wedges and stir fry;"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sprinkle in the sugar and continue stir-frying"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "until the tomatoes soften and release a large amount of juice;"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Return the egg pieces to the pan, add salt, reduce to low heat;"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Gently toss everything together until the sauce evenly coats the egg pieces;"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Once the sauce thickens slightly, turn off the heat, plate, and garnish with green onion."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-4c4c68acded8f6a2"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Yes, this is nothing more than a recipe for Tomato and Egg Stir-Fry, the most ordinary of\nhome-cooked dishes.\nPerhaps you were expecting something else,\nbut, if you'll humor an old ramble from Arita...\nNo myths or lengends can hold a candle to a simple recipe of a home-cooked dish.\nO greatest of treasure hunters!\nDo not let the Elations of others\nlead your heart astray!"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-63032ad7c645cc2d"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
